[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Offline use and refresh

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-030
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Read offline
STATEMENT: >>>
Without a connection the app shall show the agenda and tasks from its local cache and show that it is offline.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-031
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Queue changes offline
STATEMENT: >>>
Creating tasks and agenda items and completing tasks without a connection shall be queued and sent to the server when the connection returns.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Editing and deleting existing items needs a connection.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-032
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Automatic refresh
STATEMENT: >>>
While the agenda or tasks screen is open, the app shall refresh its data every minute; the user can also pull to refresh.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: AI buddy

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-050
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AI buddy tab
STATEMENT: >>>
The bottom navigation shall show a third destination 'AI buddy' next to 'Agenda' and 'Taken' only while the backend reports the AI buddy as configured (REQ-BE-083); otherwise the navigation shows only 'Agenda' and 'Taken'. The app checks this at start-up and with every automatic refresh (REQ-MOB-032). When the AI buddy becomes unavailable while its tab is open, the app switches to 'Agenda'.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Messenger-style chat
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy tab shall show the conversation like a messenger app: the user's messages as bubbles on the right, the AI buddy's on the left, each with its time, the newest at the bottom, and a text field with a send button at the bottom. On opening, the app loads the conversation from the backend (REQ-BE-087) and scrolls to the newest message.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-050
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-087

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-052
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Typing indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
While the app waits for the AI buddy's answer, it shall show a bubble on the left with animated dots, as messenger apps do when the other side is typing. The send button is disabled until the answer or an error arrives.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-053
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Errors and offline
STATEMENT: >>>
The chat needs a connection. When the phone is offline or the backend returns an error, the app shall show the Dutch error message below the user's message with a 'Opnieuw' button that sends the message again. Chat messages are not queued for later like other changes (REQ-MOB-031).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-054
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Refresh after changes
STATEMENT: >>>
After each answer of the AI buddy, the app shall refresh its agenda and task data, so that changes made by the AI buddy (REQ-BE-089) show in the Agenda and Taken tabs right away.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-050
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-089

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-055
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Clear the conversation
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy tab shall have an action to clear the conversation, after a confirmation. It clears the conversation on the backend for all of the user's devices.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-056
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Voice input
STATEMENT: >>>
While the text field of the AI buddy chat is empty, the send button shall be replaced by a microphone button, as in messenger apps. Tapping it starts speech recognition in Dutch through the phone's speech recognition service, independent of the keyboard. While listening:

- the button shows that the app is listening (animated, with a stop icon) and the text field shows 'Luisteren…';
- the recognised text appears in the text field as the user speaks;
- recognition stops after a pause in speaking, or when the user taps the button again.

After recognition stops, the text stays in the text field, where the user can change it and send it with the send button, unless sending automatically is switched on (REQ-MOB-057). Nothing recognised leaves the field empty. The first use asks for microphone permission. When permission is refused, or the phone has no speech recognition, the app shows a Dutch message ('Spraakherkenning is niet beschikbaar op dit toestel' or 'Geef de app toegang tot de microfoon om in te spreken') and the chat keeps working by typing. The microphone button is disabled while the app waits for an answer (REQ-MOB-052).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One tap from the chat instead of opening the keyboard's voice input, with the text visible and correctable before the AI buddy acts on it.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Audio goes to the phone's speech recognition service (on most phones Google's), not to the backend or the AI buddy, unless an offline Dutch language pack is installed on the phone; this is the same as the keyboard's voice input.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-057
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Send voice messages automatically
STATEMENT: >>>
The menu of the AI buddy tab shall have an on/off option 'Spraak direct versturen', off by default. When on, the recognised text is sent as soon as recognition stops (REQ-MOB-056), without tapping send; nothing recognised sends nothing. The setting is stored on the device and kept after restarting the app.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-056

[[/SECTION]]

